    dict(key='09-act-2-figure', kind='figure', title='How 287082 is made',
         body='code_steps',
         narration="So how is two eight seven, zero eight two made? [[slnc 400]] The library hides it, so a small class does it by hand, in four steps. [[slnc 600]] Step one. [[slnc 300]] Fifty nine divided by thirty is one, dropping the remainder. [[slnc 300]] That step number is written as eight bytes: seven zeros, then a one. [[slnc 600]] Step two. [[slnc 300]] H M A C mixes the secret key with those eight bytes, using S H A one. [[slnc 300]] Out come twenty bytes, which nobody can make without the key. [[slnc 600]] Step three. [[slnc 300]] Look at the last byte, a b. [[slnc 300]] Its last half, b, is eleven. [[slnc 300]] So take four bytes, starting at byte eleven: c one, three nine, seven e, e a. [[slnc 600]] Step four. [[slnc 300]] Drop the top bit, so the number is never negative, and read it as a number. [[slnc 300]] Keep the last six digits: two eight seven, zero eight two. [[slnc 300]] Exactly the library's code."),
    dict(key='10-act-2', kind='console', title='Act Two — How the code at time 59 is made, step by step',
         body='TWO. How the code at time 59 is made, step by step.\n  STEP 1. THE TIME STEP = 59 / 30, AS 8 BYTES:\n    step      1\n    counter   00000000 00000001\n  STEP 2. HMAC-SHA1(key, counter) = 20 BYTES:\n    hmac      75a48a19 d4cbe100 644e8ac1 397eea74 7a2d33ab\n  STEP 3. TAKE 4 BYTES, FROM THE LAST HALF-BYTE ON:\n    last      ab, so offset 11\n    4 bytes   c1397eea\n  STEP 4. DROP THE TOP BIT, KEEP THE LAST 6 DIGITS:\n    number    1094287082\n    code      287082\n  the same code the library gave: true',
         narration='Here are the same four steps, printed by the program. [[slnc 300]] The last line checks the result against the library. [[slnc 200]] True.'),
