    dict(key='24-class-2', kind='code', title="OtpService — the library's one line",
         body="// OtpService: the bank's check, around the library\n// make a code\nreturn generator.generateOneTimePasswordString(key,\n        Instant.ofEpochSecond(unixSeconds));\n...\n// check a code, for one step only\nreturn generator.validateOneTimePassword(key,\n        Instant.ofEpochSecond(unixSeconds), code);",
         narration="O T P service is the bank's code. [[slnc 300]] Making a code is one call to the library. [[slnc 300]] Checking a code, for one step, is another."),
    dict(key='25-class-3', kind='code', title='OtpService — the window and the replay memory',
         body="// OtpService: the bank's check, around the library\nlong current = now / stepSeconds;\nfor (long step = current - window; step <= current + window; step++) {\n    if (step >= 0 && libraryValidates(key, step * stepSeconds, code)) {\n        if (replayProtection && step <= lastStep.getOrDefault(user, -1L)) {\n            return Result.REPLAYED;\n        }\n        lastStep.put(user, step);\n        return Result.OK;",
         narration="Verify is what the bank adds. [[slnc 300]] It asks the library about each step in the window, one either side. [[slnc 300]] If a step matches but is not newer than the customer's last one, it is replayed. [[slnc 300]] Otherwise it remembers the step, and says O K."),
    dict(key='26-class-4', kind='code', title='TotpSteps — the four steps',
         body='// TotpSteps: works out the code by hand\n// step 1: which 30-second step, as 8 bytes\nlong step = unixSeconds / 30;\nbyte[] counter = ByteBuffer.allocate(8).putLong(step).array();\n// step 2: HMAC-SHA1 with the key, 20 bytes\nbyte[] hmac = hmacSha1(key, counter);\n// step 3: the last half-byte says where to take 4 bytes\nint offset = hmac[hmac.length - 1] & 0x0f;\nint fourBytes = ByteBuffer.wrap(hmac, offset, 4).getInt();\n// step 4: drop the top bit, keep the last 6 digits\nint number = fourBytes & 0x7fffffff;\nString code = String.format("%06d", number % 1_000_000);',
         narration="T O T P steps does the four steps of act two by hand. [[slnc 300]] The step number as eight bytes. [[slnc 200]] The H M A C. [[slnc 200]] Four bytes, picked by the last half byte. [[slnc 200]] And the last six digits. [[slnc 300]] A test checks it gives the library's exact code."),
